 "text": "Hey there, how are you feeling? Drawing is really fun anyone starts, and there's no shame in not being born with a pretty line. Pick up few basic techniques if you like, or just skip them and draw from life instead. Find a basic sketchbook that you enjoy using. Full sketchbook is great for keeping your activities together, a small portable one is useful on outings, and an electronic drawing tablet is different. Don't worry about it. Start with simple lines rather than fixing up bad ones, and keep practicing every day. A few weeks of quick drawing will surprise you. Hand and arm get used to basic drawing very",
